# Divided power envelopes

Let `(A, I, γ)` be a divided power ring, let `f : A → B` be a ring homomorphism, and let
`J ⊆ B` be an ideal containing `f(I)`.  The divided power envelope `D_B(J)` is a divided power
ring over `A` together with a map of ring--ideal pairs `(B, J) → (D, I_D)`, universal among
divided power rings over `A`: restriction along that map identifies divided power morphisms
`D → C` over `A` with morphisms of pairs `(B, J) → (C, I_C)` over `(A, I)`.

The envelope is constructed from the universal property rather than written down: the functor
of compatible maps out of `(A, I)` and `(B, J)` preserves limits and has a solution set of
bounded cardinality, so Brown representability for divided power rings corepresents it.

Two further properties of the construction are proved here.  Forming the envelope commutes with
taking quotients: for a surjection `B' → B`, the envelope over `B` is the quotient of the
envelope over `B'` by the divided power ideal generated by the kernel.  And it commutes with a
base change `B → B'` which is flat modulo the divided power ideal and has no first Tor
obstruction.

The envelope also factors the quotient map of `B` by `J`: there is a unique ring map
`D → B ⧸ J` restricting to that quotient map along `B → D`, it is a map over `A`, and its
kernel is the divided power ideal of `D`.

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.IdealPair.Hom` — a ring homomorphism carrying one specified ideal into another.
* `Crystalline.IdealPair.HomOver` — such a morphism together with a factorization through a
  fixed morphism out of the source pair.
* `Crystalline.DividedPowerEnvelope` — a divided power ring over `A`, its structural maps, and
  the universal Hom equivalence that characterizes it.
* `Crystalline.dividedPowerKernelIdeal` — the ideal of an envelope generated by all positive
  divided powers of the image of the kernel of a ring homomorphism.
* `Crystalline.baseChangeDPMorphism` — the canonical divided power morphism between the two
  envelopes occurring in a base change.

## Main results

* `Crystalline.dividedPowerEnvelope` — the divided power envelope exists.
* `Crystalline.dividedPowerEnvelope_factorization` — the quotient map `B → B ⧸ J` factors
  through the envelope, with the divided power ideal as the kernel of the second map.
* `Crystalline.dividedPowerEnvelope_quotient` — for a surjection `B′ → B` the canonical map of
  envelopes is surjective with kernel `dividedPowerKernelIdeal`.
* `Crystalline.dividedPowerEnvelope_baseChange` — the base-changed envelope is the envelope of
  the base-changed ideal.

## Implementation notes

The displayed equality of Hom sets in the source is represented by an equivalence; the
`homEquiv_apply` field of `DividedPowerEnvelope` says that the equivalence is exactly
restriction along the canonical map from `(B, J)`, rather than an arbitrary bijection, so that
it is automatically natural in the target divided power algebra.  The base and its algebra may
lie in independent universes; the envelope and the target divided power algebras lie in their
common ambient universe, and the universe lifts needed by the construction are internal, so the
structural map and the universal property are stated for the original base.

Because envelopes are specified by a universal property rather than chosen definitionally, the
quotient description is expressed through the unique canonical surjective divided power
morphism together with the computation of its kernel, and the base-change description through a
ring equivalence whose value on pure tensors is the canonical map supplied by the universal
property.

